<!--Post: 4439--><!--Time: 1106362161-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4439"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iceteajan<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iceteajan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 21, 2005 - 6:49 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Only three things come to my mind: <BR> <BR>Blood Relative&#40;s&#41; <BR>Perhaps he has family here, or perhaps even a family member passed away recently and willed property to him &#40;so he came back either to live in the property or sell it&#41;. <BR> <BR>A “Signifcant Other” that is his “cover” and possibly his only life line for continued survival <BR>Perhaps he lives with someone who he relies on heavily for his “cover”.  This person may have provided LONG-TERM windowdressing for BTK by maintaining a very normal lifestyle.  BTK could just simply be living “behind” this person. <BR> <BR>Long-Term Permanent Job <BR>Perhaps he has a job in Wichita &#40;or based in Wichita&#41; that he invested his life into.  A job that he could never easily acquire anywhere else in the US &#40;given his current age, his skills or lack of skills, or his citizenship or lack thereof&#41;. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4439-->
<!--Post: 4466--><!--Time: 1106393950-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4466"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nugzter<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nugzter<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 22, 2005 - 3:39 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think something bad happened to him in Wichita that also had something to do with WPD. Had to have happened when he was very young. As he got older and being very intellegent he is paying those back who done him wrong.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4466-->
<!--Post: 4475--><!--Time: 1106401511-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4475"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 22, 2005 - 5:45 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->While the idea of BTK being a cop isn&#39;t top on my BTK job/profession list, it&#39;s one of only a few theories, occupation-wise, which I think has a kernel of considerable plausibility to it; but it&#39;s easy to fall into that trap; if BTK was a cop, it explains almost all questions. He may have tried to become a cop, but failed. He is attracted to order and discipline. He could be a security guard or a wannabe cop, too. Nugzter, I know you&#39;re saying other than what I just wrote. When you mentioned WPD this idea took hold of me a minute ago.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
