<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4534"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Stealth<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Stealth<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 23, 2005 - 9:06 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->&#34;i believe he has been in prison for other crimes and was recently released&#34; <BR> <BR>There is fingerprint and DNA evidence.  If he was in prison, they could match up his fingerprints.  So prison is very unlikely. <BR>Also, a few years back, most states started taking DNA samples of inmates.   <BR> <BR>If he was doing the same thing other places, they would be able to tie it to BTK through DNA &#40;semen, hair, epithelial&#41;, fingerprint, or MO/signature. <BR> <BR>I think the violence regression is what makes BTK somewhat unique.  <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
