<!--Post: 4539--><!--Time: 1106507160-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4539"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iceteajan<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iceteajan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 23, 2005 - 11:06 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Metalhead &amp; Stealth: <BR> <BR>There was another thread I started about fingerprints and the military. <BR> <BR>We thought perhaps BTK was in the miltary and therefore some comparisons could be made to the fingerprint &#40;?or partial fingerprint?&#41; that was supposedly left on a chair &#40;?at the Oteros?&#41;. <BR> <BR>That is a good point about someone who enjoys killing -- why should he stop for 25 years and then all of the sudden start taunting the police again with old momentos? <BR> <BR>Perhaps he was on some kind of medication &#40;available through his employer&#39;s health insurance&#41; that stabilized him sufficiently through those quiet years.  Now, that he is older and retired he may no longer be able to afford or be entitled to this medication. <BR> <BR>Also, now that he is older, he doesn&#39;t have enough of that &#34;sexual whatever&#34; urging him to kill for this pleasure. <BR> <BR>He may only have just has enough strength to taunt &#40;and live through&#41; his old conquests.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
