<!--Post: 4542--><!--Time: 1106511524-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4542"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dpinva<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dpinva<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 23, 2005 - 12:18 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Or Ice, he simply never stopped and either went elsewhere or changed his signature and MO. This maniac is smart enough for anything to be a possibility.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4542-->
<!--Post: 4547--><!--Time: 1106516157-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4547"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Stealth<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Stealth<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 23, 2005 - 1:35 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Fingerprint evidence that seems to be a fact: The previously mentioned chair, one of the bags, and one of the letters. Possible: Otero&#39;s car. Until the police tell us for sure, it&#39;s all speculation. The police have stated several times they have &#34;fingerprint&#34; evidence. <BR> <BR>It is always possible none of the fingerprints are BTK&#39;s.  It is also possible his fingerprints are on file somewhere but aren&#39;t in the IAFIS for whatever reason &#40;age?&#41;.  In one of the 1974 articles I read on this case, the WPD announced they were going to start fingerprinting everyone arrested. They didn&#39;t before??? <BR> <BR>Most likely he has never been arrested for a major crime or ever been in the military - IceIceBaby said&#40;I was in the military and one of the first things they do is finger print you&#41;. <BR> <BR>The DNA collection of prisoners is very new and most likely of no help even if he ever had been in prison. <BR> <BR>The police and BTK have so far attributed only the ones we know.  Given what we know, it appears he has stayed in the area and has been dormant.  Speculation is often much more exciting than the reality. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
